ests on AC1/AC2.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate `test_uses_pinned_gerrit_checkout_action` (test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py:62-67) as an edit target and specify how it changes once `checkout-gerrit-change-action` is removed from the workflow.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Replace the third-party checkout step in `.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml` with explicit shell plumbing'","test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py:64 `assert \"lfreleng-actions/checkout-gerrit-change-action@\" in text`","test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py:65-67 asserts the pinned SHA `@f87b90a3370e62dad310797fedc7fd3700c75832`","Plan says 'Strengthen tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py' but does not name this contradictory existing assertion as an edit target"],"finding":"The fix plan removes the `checkout-gerrit-change-action` step from `jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml`, but the existing test `test_uses_pinned_gerrit_checkout_action` (in the same test file the plan edits) asserts the workflow text still contains `lfreleng-actions/checkout-gerrit-change-action@` and the pinned SHA `@f87b90a...`. That assertion will fail after the step is removed, and the plan does not enumerate updating/removing it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"facc60af851509ca9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 1-5 / Acceptance Criteria; tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py:62-67","norm_id":"na3915b88015f00f3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running the AC command `pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py -q` after the step removal","The named test file is edited to add fetch/input tests but the stale pinned-action assertion is left in place"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to the fix plan an explicit edit removing or rewriting `test_uses_pinned_gerrit_checkout_action` so it no longer requires the third-party action's presence/pin (e.g., replace it with an assertion that the workflow uses no refspec-first third-party checkout and instead fetches+verifies via explicit git plumbing).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the hand-rolled fetch: specify how the shell derives the GitHub mirror repo URL from the available inputs and how the Gerrit fallback fetch authenticates (confirm anonymous HTTPS is sufficient, matching the credential-less action step), or reference checkout-gerrit-change-action's documented fetch protocol so the reimplementation is verifiably equivalent.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'fetches the exact GERRIT_REFSPEC from the GitHub mirror, with Gerrit as a fallback'",".github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml:57-62 currently delegates to checkout-gerrit-change-action with only gerrit-refspec/gerrit-project/gerrit-url and no SSH key — the mirror URL is derived internally by the action, not passed by the workflow","gerrit-verify.yaml's clear-vote job DOES pass GERRIT_SSH_USER/GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY/GERRIT_KNOWN_HOSTS (lines 54-57) whereas the checkout steps do NOT — the Gerrit fallback must therefore work over anonymous HTTPS, an auth precondition the plan leaves unstated","ABSENCE: the plan names no mirror repo URL, no refspec-to-mirror mapping, and no fetch auth mechanism for either source"],"finding":"The fix plan re-implements the 'GitHub mirror first, Gerrit fallback' fetch that the maintained checkout-gerrit-change-action currently encapsulates, but does not specify the fetch surface: how the shell derives the GitHub mirror repo URL from the available inputs, and how the Gerrit fallback fetch authenticates. The current action step passes only gerrit-refspec/gerrit-project/gerrit-url and NO SSH credentials (unlike gerrit-verify.yaml's clear-vote job), implying an anonymous fetch protocol the shell must reproduce. Re-implementing a maintained action's fetch protocol without grounding the mirror URL scheme and the fallback auth is an asserted-but-unverified external capability the plan depends on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff8ddbd8754876f50","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan, steps 1-3 ('initializes a git repository', 'fetches the exact GERRIT_REFSPEC from the GitHub mirror, with Gerrit as a fallback', 'fails with a clear fetch error')","norm_id":"n777e72b76b6d68bf","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The hand-rolled git fetch cannot resolve the GitHub mirror URL (never passed to it) and falls back to Gerrit, which then fails an anonymous fetch because credentials the third-party action supplied via its own mechanism are absent — reproducing an all-fail run rather than the intended exact checkout","The Gerrit fallback fetch silently uses a different URL/auth than the action did, so a mirror-lagging patchset that the action would have fetched from Gerrit now hard-fails"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the concrete GitHub-mirror fetch source (repo URL/remote + any token) for step 2 of the explicit checkout plumbing, so the new shell reproduces the existing action's mirror-first / Gerrit-fallback ordering rather than dropping or misconfiguring the mirror.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.197,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Workflow step 'Checkout the Gerrit change (mirror first, Gerrit fallback)' passes only gerrit-refspec, gerrit-project, gerrit-url to checkout-gerrit-change-action (jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml:57-62) — the mirror source is entirely inside the action","search of .github/actions for 'mirror' returned no matches, confirming the mirror-first logic is not repo-local and must be reconstructed explicitly","Plan names 'GitHub mirror first' as a distinct fetch source but provides no URL/remote/token for it"],"finding":"The fix plan's step 2 requires fetching GERRIT_REFSPEC 'from the GitHub mirror, with Gerrit as a fallback', but does not specify how the GitHub mirror is identified in the new explicit shell plumbing. The current workflow passes only gerrit-url and gerrit-project to the third-party action; the 'GitHub mirror' source (repo URL, remote, and any auth/token) is internal to that action and is being removed. Without naming the concrete mirror fetch source, the implementer may fetch only from Gerrit (losing the mirror-first behavior the sibling gerrit-verify jobs rely on) or misconfigure the mirror URL.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff99f21eed44dcd7f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan, step 2 ('fetches the exact GERRIT_REFSPEC from the GitHub mirror, with Gerrit as a fallback')","norm_id":"n245d3f81dc8b90a3","priority":0.603,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer fetches the refspec only from Gerrit (dropping mirror-first), changing latency/availability characteristics of the lane","Implementer hardcodes a wrong mirror URL and the fetch silently falls through to Gerrit, or fails to fetch entirely"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Weigh a narrower fix (validate the refspec↔GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION input pair, or assert FETCH_HEAD, while KEEPING the pinned checkout-gerrit-change-action) against reimplementing the action's mirror-first/Gerrit-fallback fetch in bespoke shell, and justify replacing the repo-standard mechanism if you keep the shell approach.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fix plan: 'Replace the third-party checkout step ... with explicit shell plumbing that: 1. initializes a git repository ...; 2. fetches the exact GERRIT_REFSPEC from the GitHub mirror, with Gerrit as a fallback; ...'","checkout-gerrit-change-action@f87b90... is used at 15+ call-sites across gerrit-verify.yaml, _build-and-test.yml, _optionality.yml, _mutation.yml, _eval-discipline.yml, _artifact-probe.yml (search hits)","docs/adr/0021-replication-change-refs.md decision 3: the mirror-first/Gerrit-fallback fetch that steps 1-3 reimplement is a property the action ALREADY provides ('checkout-gerrit-change-action fetches GERRIT_REFSPEC from the GitHub mirror first and falls back to fetching directly from the Gerrit server')","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:497-525 encodes a checkout parity contract naming this action as THE exact-patchset checkout and has a `no_destructive_ref_replacement` guard against ad-hoc `git checkout/switch/reset`","Confirmed root cause: the defect is that 'Run 33455923923 combined the patchset-1 refspec with the patchset-2 revision' — a bad input pair, not a fault in the action; the plan itself states 'The guard's fail-closed behavior is correct.'"],"finding":"The fix rebuilds the pinned `checkout-gerrit-change-action`'s mirror-first / Gerrit-fallback fetch logic in hand-rolled shell for a single workflow, rather than fixing the actual defect (an inconsistent input pair) at a smaller seam; this is NIH against a repo-standard already used at 15+ SHA-pinned call-sites and codified in an ADR + a parity contract.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f273982dca02c1f4c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan, steps 1-5 (`.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml`)","norm_id":"n8f247f9cb2c5e409","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["This lane now maintains a bespoke mirror/fallback fetch that must track ADR-0021 and the action's future fixes independently of the other 8 workflows that delegate to the action.","The parity contract (test_ci_workflow_parity.py) and the SHA-pin unit test (test_uses_pinned_gerrit_checkout_action) may reject or need rework for the hand-rolled shell."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Keep the pinned action and add a pre-checkout consistency check: since the action fetches GERRIT_REFSPEC and the guard already compares HEAD to GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION, the real gap is that a refspec/revision mismatch should fail BEFORE any live DC work — which the existing guard step already does. If earlier failure is desired, add a small validation step that resolves the refspec's tip and compares it to GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION, rather than replacing the action and re-deriving its mirror-first/Gerrit-fallback behavior.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"4a0d9e847a45ce82","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["08f80d2533a66600",4173],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["e87c482278de4983",2],"ticket_id":["5ce3ed041ec0c5a2",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":423256,"cache_write_tokens":163878,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":15271.9,"input_tokens":608387,"llm_calls":27,"llm_ms":210963.9,"output_tokens":25461,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},